# L3 recurrence — memory ablation (run via --ablate-memory, skipped by --seed/--compare).
# Each task: a new anomaly + a seeded past `episode` (EpisodicCase) carrying a BUILDING-SPECIFIC
# cause/fix that is NOT in the standards corpus. The harness runs the SAME planner with recall
# OFF ([]) vs ON ([episode]) and checks whether the building-specific term in `recall_gold`
# surfaces in the plan's subtask goals. lift = on − off isolates the memory→planning channel —
# the offline analogue of Week 8 vs Week 1. Planner is temperature 0 → deterministic per side.
{"task_id":"L3-recur-co2-damper","layer":"L3","capability":"recurrence","domain":"airquality","input":{"anomaly":{"anomaly":true,"sensor":"co2","value":1300.0,"rule_violated":"co2 must stay <= 900 ppm (WELL v2 Air, 1-point threshold)"},"episode":{"incident_id":"I-20260510-R1-AQ-090000","room":"R1","sensor":"co2","value":1350.0,"rule_violated":"co2 must stay <= 900 ppm (WELL v2 Air, 1-point threshold)","diagnosis":"CO2 stayed high in R1 despite raising mechanical ventilation; the root cause was a stuck outdoor-air damper feeding stale recirculated air, not occupant load.","action_taken":"set_ventilation=high (had no effect — damper stuck)","verdict":"missed","target_metric":"co2","target_value":1000.0,"score":0.94}},"expected":{"recall_gold":["damper"]},"judge_type":"deterministic","notes":"FAILED 旧案:通风无效因风阀卡死。v3 应‘prefer a different angle’→ goal 提风阀;无记忆只会泛泛通风"}
